  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "In the number \\(74982.1035\\) the value of the place occupied by the digit \\(9\\) is how many times as great as the value of the place occupied by the digit \\(3?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1{,}000\\)",
    "B": "\\(10{,}000\\)",
    "C": "\\(100{,}000\\)",
    "D": "\\(1{,}000{,}000\\)",
    "E": "\\(10{,}000{,}000\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The digit \\(9\\) occupies the hundreds place, whose value is \\(100\\). The digit \\(3\\) occupies the thousandths place, whose value is \\(0.001\\).\n\nThe requested factor is the quotient of these place values. Multiply both the dividend and divisor by \\(1000\\) to make the divisor \\(1\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{100}{0.001}\n=\\frac{100\\cdot1000}{0.001\\cdot1000}\n=\\boxed{100{,}000}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
